Select the most appropriate output for the below C program.

- `1 1 1 2 2 1 2 2`
- `1 1 1 2`
- `1 1 1 2 2 1`
- Infinite loop

```c
#include <stdio.h>
int main() {
    int i = 1, j = 1;
    while (i <= 2) {
        while (j <= 2) {
            printf("%d %d ", i, j);
            j++;
        }
        i++;
    }
    return 0;
}
```

Analyze the C code below and select the correct output.

- `321`
- `32`
- `3210`
- `21`

```c
#include <stdio.h>
int main() {
    int ans=0;
    for(int i=0;i<=10;i++){
        if(i%2==0) continue;
        ans+=i;
    }
    printf("%d",ans);
    return 0;
}
```

